-- The public authorities these Regulations name and give things to do or to receive.  Reg 7(1)
-- makes some of them supervisory authorities; reg 3(1) names the others ("the NCA", "the
-- PRA", "Department for the Economy"); regs 8(3), 63 and 74 name the rest.  A supervisory
-- authority is therefore a value of this type picked out by reg 7, not a type of its own.
-- src:200 | (1) Subject to paragraph (2), the following bodies are supervisory authorities in relation to relevant persons—
-- src:201 | (a) the FCA is the supervisory authority for—
-- src:202 | (i) credit and financial institutions (including money service businesses) which are authorised persons but not excluded money service businesses;
-- src:203 | (ii) trust or company service providers which are authorised persons;
-- src:204 | (iii) Annex 1 financial institutions;
-- src:205 | (iv) electronic money institutions;
-- src:206 | (v) auction platforms;
-- src:207 | (vi) credit unions in Northern Ireland;
-- src:208 | (vii) recognised investment exchanges within the meaning of section 285 of FSMA (exemption for recognised investment exchanges , clearing houses and central securities depositories);
-- src:209 | (viii) cryptoasset exchange providers;
-- src:210 | (ix) custodian wallet providers;
-- src:211 | (b) each of the professional bodies listed in Schedule 1 is the supervisory authority for relevant persons who are members of it, or regulated or supervised by it;
-- src:212 | (c) the Commissioners are the supervisory authority for—
-- src:213 | (i) high value dealers;
-- src:214 | (ii) money service businesses which are not supervised by the FCA;
-- src:215 | (iii) trust or company service providers which are not supervised by the FCA or one of the professional bodies listed in Schedule 1;
-- src:216 | (iv) auditors, external accountants and tax advisers who are not supervised by one of the professional bodies listed in Schedule 1;
-- src:217 | (v) bill payment service providers which are not supervised by the FCA;
-- src:218 | (vi) telecommunication, digital and IT payment service providers which are not supervised by the FCA;
-- src:219 | (vii) estate agents and letting agents which are not supervised by one of the professional bodies listed in Schedule 1;
-- src:220 | (viii) art market participants;
-- src:221 | (d) the Gambling Commission is the supervisory authority for casinos.
@ref reg 7(1) (src:200-221)
DECLARE Authority IS ONE OF
    `the Financial Conduct Authority`
    `the Prudential Regulation Authority`
    `the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
    `the Gambling Commission`
    `the National Crime Agency`
    `the Treasury`
    `the Department for the Economy in Northern Ireland`
    `a local weights and measures authority`
    `a professional body listed in Schedule 1` HAS `which body` IS A `Professional body`

-- What a customer, or the owner of a firm, IS: the legal form that regs 5 and 6 sort on.
-- "Body corporate" (reg 3(1)) includes a company and a limited liability partnership and
-- excludes a corporation sole and a partnership that is not a body corporate.
DECLARE `Form of customer` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a company`
    `a limited liability partnership`
    `a body corporate of another kind`
    `a corporation sole`
    `a partnership other than a limited liability partnership`
    `an unincorporated association`
    `a trust`
    `a foundation or other legal arrangement similar to a trust`
    `the estate of a deceased person in the course of administration`
    `another legal entity or legal arrangement`

-- The three jurisdictions inside the United Kingdom where the Regulations say something
-- different (reg 6(6), the courts and registrars in regs 29, 30A and Parts 8 to 10).
DECLARE `Part of the United Kingdom` IS ONE OF
    `England and Wales`
    `Scotland`
    `Northern Ireland`

§ `The things the Regulations are about`

-- The customer, as the facts a relevant person can state about it.
DECLARE Customer HAS
    `form of the customer`                          IS A `Form of customer`
    `securities listed on a regulated market`       IS A BOOLEAN -- regs 5(1), 28(5), 37(3)(a)(iv): a company's securities
    `beneficially owned by another person`          IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 28(4)
    `a person purports to act on its behalf`        IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 28(10)

-- One transaction, or a run of linked operations taken together.
DECLARE Transaction HAS
    `value in sterling, linked operations taken together`    IS A NUMBER  -- pounds sterling (reg 3(2))
    `paid in cash`                                           IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 3(1) "cash"
    `carried out as part of a business relationship`         IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 3(1) "occasional transaction" is the opposite
    `a transfer of funds under the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN -- Article 3.9 of that regulation (regs 27(1)(b), 64A(2))

-- Reg 64B: a cryptoasset transfer is one of two kinds.
DECLARE `Kind of cryptoasset transfer` IS ONE OF
    `an inter-cryptoasset business transfer`
    `an unhosted wallet transfer`

DECLARE `Cryptoasset transfer` HAS
    `kind of transfer`                                          IS A `Kind of cryptoasset transfer`
    `value in sterling, linked transfers taken together`        IS A NUMBER -- the sterling equivalent (regs 27(7E), 64C(4), 64G(1)(b))

-- The three things a risk assessment is about (regs 16A, 18A, 19A and Part 3).
DECLARE `Kind of risk` IS ONE OF
    `money laundering`
    `terrorist financing`
    `proliferation financing`

-- A level of risk, as the relevant person has assessed it (regs 28(12), 30(3), 33(1)(a), 37(1)).
DECLARE `Level of risk` IS ONE OF
    `high risk`
    `low risk`
    `neither high nor low risk`

-- Schedule 2: the activities a financial institution carries on (reg 10(2)(a) and (4)(a)).
-- THE RENDERING SHOWS 13 UNNUMBERED ITEMS, the first of them "Lending"; reg 10(4)(a) speaks of
-- "points 2 to 12, 14 and 15".  The points cannot be matched to items from this text, so the
-- items are named, in the order printed, and never numbered here (see PLAN.md).
-- src:2980 | The activities ... are—
-- src:2981 | Lending including, inter alia: consumer credit, credit agreements relating to immovable property, factoring, with or without recourse, financing of commercial transactions (including forfeiting).
-- src:2982 | Financial leasing.
-- src:2983 | Payment services as defined in regulation 2(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017, other than an account information service (within the meaning of that term in regulation 2(1) of those Regulations).
-- src:2984 | Issuing and administering other means of payment (e.g. travellers' cheques and bankers' drafts) ....
-- src:2985 | Guarantees and commitments.
-- src:2986 | Trading for own account or for account of customers in any of the following:
-- src:2987 | (a) money market instruments (cheques, bills, certificates of deposit, etc.);
-- src:2988 | (b) foreign exchange;
-- src:2989 | (c) financial futures and options;
-- src:2990 | (d) exchange and interest-rate instruments;
-- src:2991 | (e) transferable securities.
-- src:2992 | Participation in securities issues and the provision of services relating to such issues.
-- src:2993 | Advice to undertakings on capital structure, industrial strategy and related questions and advice as well as services relating to mergers and the purchase of undertakings.
-- src:2994 | Money broking.
-- src:2995 | Portfolio management and advice.
-- src:2996 | Safekeeping and administration of securities.
-- src:2997 | Safe custody services.
-- src:2998 | Issuing electronic money.
@ref sch 2 (src:2980-2998)
DECLARE `Listed activity` IS ONE OF
    `lending`
    `financial leasing`
    `payment services`
    `issuing and administering other means of payment`
    `guarantees and commitments`
    `trading for own account or for account of customers`
    `participation in securities issues and related services`
    `advice to undertakings on capital structure, industrial strategy and mergers`
    `money broking`
    `portfolio management and advice`
    `safekeeping and administration of securities`
    `safe custody services`
    `issuing electronic money`

§ `Shared constants`

-- Reg 1(2).  Read by provisions that count from, or look back to, the day the Regulations
-- came into force (text lines 639, 886-894, 1142, 1858, 2009).
-- src:9 | (2) These Regulations come into force on 26th June 2017.
@ref reg 1(2) (src:9)
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 1(2) the date these Regulations came into force` MEANS Date 26 6 2017

-- The figure £800, used in four places as a threshold on a transfer: regs 27(1)(b)
-- ("exceeding"), 27(7E), 64C(4) and 64G(1)(b) ("equal to or exceeds").  Kept here once so
-- the four cannot drift apart; each part chooses its own comparison.
-- src:767 | (b) carries out an occasional transaction that amounts to a transfer of funds within the meaning of Article 3.9 of the funds transfer regulation exceeding £800;
-- src:791 | (7E) Without prejudice to paragraph (7D), a cryptoasset exchange provider and a custodian wallet provider must also apply customer due diligence measures in relation to a cryptoasset transfer which is equal to or exceeds the equivalent in cryptoassets of £800 in value (taken together with any other cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked).
@ref regs 27(1)(b) and 27(7E) (src:767) (src:791)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the transfer threshold of 800 pounds sterling` MEANS 800
